-- title:
--   Germ at x of the vanishing ideal of ξ̄ is the branch ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme, let $\xi, x$ be points of $X$ with $h$ a witness that $\xi$ specialises to $x$ (i.e. $x$ lies in the closure of $\{\xi\}$), let $U$ be an affine open of $X$, and suppose $x \in U$. Consider the ideal sheaf data obtained as `Scheme.IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal` of the closed set $\overline{\{\xi\}}$ (closed as the closure of a set), and take its component over $U$, an ideal of the ring $\Gamma(X, U)$. The assertion is that the ideal of the local ring $\mathcal O_{X,x}$ generated by the image of this ideal under the germ map $\Gamma(X, U) \to \mathcal O_{X,x}$ at $x$ (the `Ideal.map` along that ring homomorphism) coincides with `Scheme.branchIdeal h`, which by definition is the preimage, under the specialisation homomorphism $\mathcal O_{X,x} \to \mathcal O_{X,\xi}$ attached to $h$, of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,\xi}$.
--
--   This identifies, in stalk terms, the ideal sheaf of the integral closed subscheme $\overline{\{\xi\}}$ with the prime of $\mathcal O_{X,x}$ consisting of germs vanishing along that branch through $x$. It is used in the analysis of the local structure of $X_1(p)$-type models at a crossing point, being cited in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.isInvertible_comap_ker_and_comap_ker_eq_prod_ofPoint_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.isInvertible_comap_ker_and_comap_ker_eq_prod_ofPoint_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
